=== Codex review finding, addressed before merge ===

Automated PR review (chatgpt-codex-connector, P1) on
services/gateway/src/frontend/command-hub/orb-widget.js:4484:
"Cancel automatic recovery when the topic breaker trips" — claimed
_enterStuckState() alone does not stop the 5s _recoveryWatchdog
health-probe (armed earlier by _announceDisconnect()), which would call
_resetAndReconnect() automatically once the (fully reachable) gateway
answers, undoing this fix within ~5s.

Verified against the code before acting (not just the claim):
$ grep -n "_recoveryWatchdog|function _announceDisconnect|function _resetAndReconnect|_disconnectActive" src/frontend/command-hub/orb-widget.js
-> confirmed _recoveryWatchdog is a real setInterval (armed in
   _announceDisconnect, ~line 1402) that calls _resetAndReconnect() on a
   successful health probe (~line 1425) whenever _s._disconnectActive is
   still true; confirmed _resetAndReconnect()'s own comment (~line 1524)
   says it deliberately relies on _disconnectActive staying true for this
   exact auto-recovery to work; confirmed _enterStuckState() (the function
   this VTID's fix calls) never touches _disconnectActive or the watchdog
   interval at all.

Finding confirmed real and applicable to this breaker (unlike
MAX_WIDGET_RECONNECTS' own use of _enterStuckState(), which fires on a
genuine unreachable-network condition where auto-recovery is desired,
this breaker fires while the gateway IS reachable — nova_validation
rejected content, not a dropped connection — so the same auto-recovery
is actively wrong here).

=== Follow-up fix ===
Edited services/gateway/src/frontend/command-hub/orb-widget.js: the
breaker block now cancels _recoveryWatchdog and clears
_s._disconnectActive before calling _enterStuckState(), so only an
explicit tap (still gated on _disconnectStuck) can resume. Deliberately
scoped to this call site only — _enterStuckState() itself and the
MAX_WIDGET_RECONNECTS call site are untouched, preserving their existing,
correct auto-recover-on-reachable behavior for real network outages.

